[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186175905 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" "question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" "question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/id #uuid "7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-103136" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡4\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $4\\pi$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\pi -2\\pi  & =2\\pi  \\\\ 2\\pi -2\\pi  & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡0=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4\\pi .$\n\nThe angle $0$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $0$ corresponds to the point $(1,0).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡0=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡0=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/id #uuid "17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7" "answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" "answer-eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299" "answer-f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70" "answer-d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7" :answer/id #uuid "0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" :answer/id #uuid "f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299" :answer/id #uuid "eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70" :answer/id #uuid "f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265" :answer/id #uuid "d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/id #uuid "8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-85510" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{11\\pi }{2}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{7\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).$\n\nThe angle $(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})$ corresponds to the point $(0,-1).$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2})=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" "answer-8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80" "answer-78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d" "answer-d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e" "answer-cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" :answer/id #uuid "be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80" :answer/id #uuid "8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d" :answer/id #uuid "78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e" :answer/id #uuid "d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427" :answer/id #uuid "cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/id #uuid "17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-103144" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{5\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}).$\n\nThe angle ${90}^{∘}$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ corresponds to the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Since the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\n- Since the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{0}{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/id #uuid "83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d" "answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" "answer-a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a" "answer-02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609" "answer-cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d" :answer/id #uuid "9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" :answer/id #uuid "a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a" :answer/id #uuid "a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609" :answer/id #uuid "02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89" :answer/id #uuid "cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175904 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/id #uuid "e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/math-academy-id "q-103159" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nThe angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ corresponds to the point $(0,1).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/id #uuid "1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2" "answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" "answer-682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8" "answer-e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8" "answer-27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2" :answer/id #uuid "37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" :answer/id #uuid "14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8" :answer/id #uuid "682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8" :answer/id #uuid "e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd" :answer/id #uuid "27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176402 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176969 :tutorial/content "For quadrantal angles that lie outside $[0^\\circ,360^\\circ),$ we first find a coterminal angle in the interval $[0^\\circ,360^\\circ),$ and then we proceed as usual. \n\nFor example, if the angle is $540^\\circ,$ then we write\n\n$$\n540^\\circ - 360^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\nSo $180^\\circ$ is coterminal with $540^\\circ,$ and we need to look at the point on the unit circle that corresponds to $180^\\circ,$ which is $(-1,0).$\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nWe can do a similar thing when working with negative angles. For example, if the angle is $-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{2},$ we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7\\pi }{2}+2\\pi  & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to look at the point that corresponds to $\\dfrac{\\pi}2,$ that is, $(0,1).$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176118 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/id #uuid "7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76"] ["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-103136"] ["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡4\\pi .$"] ["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $4\\pi$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\pi -2\\pi  & =2\\pi  \\\\ 2\\pi -2\\pi  & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡0=\\operatorname{sec}⁡4\\pi .$\n\nThe angle $0$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $0$ corresponds to the point $(1,0).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡0=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sec}⁡0=1.$"] ["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/id #uuid "17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786"] ["answer-0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7" :answer/id #uuid "0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7"] ["answer-0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" :answer/id #uuid "f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648"] ["answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299" :answer/id #uuid "eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299"] ["answer-eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70" :answer/id #uuid "f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70"] ["answer-f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70" :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}"] ["answer-d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265" :answer/id #uuid "d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265"] ["answer-d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265" :answer/value "Undefined"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/correct "answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/choices "answer-0266e39a-b3bc-5d04-b35f-a2e22e6192e7"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/choices "answer-f8dcd592-0969-561b-b975-692d2af38648"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/choices "answer-eb1bdb89-800a-5292-9e62-16895ad9e299"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/choices "answer-f335e1c9-7442-5f10-b019-8df657adad70"] ["answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786" :answer-field/choices "answer-d45f0754-1797-5dc3-99fa-a6ce96b81265"] ["question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-17a981b2-5f3e-5348-9609-333e4578b786"] [17592186175905 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7c8c6b8b-17d7-547c-9519-99c95a929f76"] ["question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/id #uuid "8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b"] ["question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-85510"] ["question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2}).$"] ["question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{11\\pi }{2}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{11\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{7\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).$\n\nThe angle $(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})$ corresponds to the point $(0,-1).$\n\nSince the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{2})=-1.$"] ["question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/id #uuid "3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9"] ["answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" :answer/id #uuid "be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b"] ["answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80" :answer/id #uuid "8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80"] ["answer-8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d" :answer/id #uuid "78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d"] ["answer-78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e" :answer/id #uuid "d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e"] ["answer-d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427" :answer/id #uuid "cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427"] ["answer-cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427" :answer/value "Undefined"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/correct "answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/choices "answer-be71c86d-3b9c-534c-a34b-4b6da4e2d78b"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/choices "answer-8e2d373f-505c-5335-8e64-76b8eb295d80"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/choices "answer-78ad4bc9-fbbe-5928-a45e-a9dc5017529d"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/choices "answer-d9b50275-efc4-5f5a-9e1f-741741a7800e"] ["answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9" :answer-field/choices "answer-cc9e04a0-d2bc-5da6-a08f-b95e6df71427"] ["question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3aaa1f21-66b6-5f2f-a870-f2d386417dc9"] [17592186175905 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8613cddf-5858-574b-9d8b-91be11b8ce7b"] ["question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/id #uuid "17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60"] ["question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-103144"] ["question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}).$"] ["question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2} \\\\ \\frac{5\\pi }{2}-2\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}).$\n\nThe angle ${90}^{∘}$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ corresponds to the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Since the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\n- Since the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}=\\frac{0}{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})=0.$"] ["question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/id #uuid "83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf"] ["answer-9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d" :answer/id #uuid "9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d"] ["answer-9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d" :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}"] ["answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" :answer/id #uuid "a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6"] ["answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a" :answer/id #uuid "a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a"] ["answer-a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609" :answer/id #uuid "02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609"] ["answer-02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609" :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}"] ["answer-cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89" :answer/id #uuid "cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89"] ["answer-cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89" :answer/value "Undefined"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/correct "answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/choices "answer-9f328edd-5cef-5843-b812-5017a9d8679d"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/choices "answer-a56dc459-8849-5b41-915a-0ec8333886c6"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/choices "answer-a899ebb2-c6bf-5cff-b840-d5e06befd72a"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/choices "answer-02586119-71be-5aa8-b399-e820d3f3c609"] ["answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf" :answer-field/choices "answer-cb513520-510e-5fbc-ae91-42c36c608b89"] ["question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-83fb8046-36a6-54cd-bf21-1210cc3f4ccf"] [17592186175905 :knowledge-point/questions "question-17db8653-72df-5afe-a4b6-7065bd849c60"] ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/id #uuid "e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901"] ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/math-academy-id "q-103159"] ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=$"] ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/worked-solution "First, we find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nThe angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ corresponds to the point $(0,1).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\nTherefore, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=0.$"] ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/id #uuid "1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59"] ["answer-37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2" :answer/id #uuid "37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2"] ["answer-37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" :answer/id #uuid "14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf"] ["answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8" :answer/id #uuid "682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8"] ["answer-682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8" :answer/id #uuid "e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8"] ["answer-e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd" :answer/id #uuid "27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd"] ["answer-27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/correct "answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/choices "answer-37a43cc4-1a56-5ea6-a470-f77306833ee2"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/choices "answer-14008af2-533f-5df0-8073-9df0dea9eabf"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/choices "answer-682f8f89-939f-5fdf-acb3-361f9eca56c8"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/choices "answer-e3a43da8-b5ab-5aec-b64f-9fe03bede5d8"] ["answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59" :answer-field/choices "answer-27daefe3-4f08-546a-b49a-e8753adc9acd"] ["question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1891b75c-a445-57bf-8516-60c344d13f59"] [17592186175904 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e8ddd7db-0156-5251-bf50-65888b2a7901"] [17592186176402 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186176969 :tutorial/content "For quadrantal angles that lie outside $[0^\\circ,360^\\circ),$ we first find a coterminal angle in the interval $[0^\\circ,360^\\circ),$ and then we proceed as usual. \n\nFor example, if the angle is $540^\\circ,$ then we write\n\n$$\n540^\\circ - 360^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\nSo $180^\\circ$ is coterminal with $540^\\circ,$ and we need to look at the point on the unit circle that corresponds to $180^\\circ,$ which is $(-1,0).$\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nWe can do a similar thing when working with negative angles. For example, if the angle is $-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{2},$ we can write \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7\\pi }{2}+2\\pi  & =-\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to look at the point that corresponds to $\\dfrac{\\pi}2,$ that is, $(0,1).$"] [17592186176118 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0]] "retractions" [[17592186176969 :tutorial/content "For quadrantal angles that lie outside $[0^\\circ,360^\\circ)$, we first find a coterminal angle in the interval $[0^\\circ,360^\\circ)$, and then we proceed as usual.\n\nFor example, if the angle is $540^\\circ$, then we write\n\n$$\n540^\\circ - 360^\\circ = 180^\\circ.\\quad{\\color{green}{\\checkmark}}\n$$\n\nSo $180^\\circ$ is coterminal with $540^\\circ$, and we need to look at the point on the unit circle that corresponds to $180^\\circ$, which is $(-1,0)$.\n\n![](images/79/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nWe can do a similar thing when working with negative angles. For example, if the angle is\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac{7π}{2} + 2π &= -\\frac{3π}{2} \\\\\n- \\frac{3π}{2} + 2π &= \\frac{π}{2}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to look at the point that corresponds to\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\pi}2\n$$\n\nthat is, $(0,1)$."]]}]